// # sec/cap — Capability Tokens
//
// Logline: The capability token system (Pillar 5). 14 NORTHSTAR core (FsRead, FsWrite, Net, Tcp, Udp, Sys, Process, Env, Time, Rand, Alloc, Thread, Gpu, Ffi) + 12 future-state (Fs, Arena, Sign, Audio, Camera, Usb, Hid, Window, Frame, Bind, CompilerRead, Metrics — the Metrics token re-uses the v2.1.0-reserved bit 0x800, added in v3.0.0 for the cap-gated oo_metrics_* family). Token derivation uses getentropy(3) — fail-closed (no LCG fallback) per NORTHSTAR. Plus the cap helpers (seal, attenuate, OoPathCap).
//
// Beats:
//   1. caps.h — the OODAR_CAP_* bit-layout and the 14 token kinds.
//   2. caps.c — orchestrator: the getentropy-derived token creation and attestation; the 26-token bit table.
//   3. cap.c — seal, attenuate, eq, plus the seccomp-bpf filter application.
//   4. cap_grant.c — oo_cap_grant (the cap-attenuation grant primitive).
//   5. cap_require.c — oo_cap_require_* family (the per-cap predicates used by every public mutator).
//   6. cap_attenuate.c — oo_cap_attenuate (the OR-mask narrowing primitive).
//
// v2.3.0 file split: the original 428-line caps.c was split into
// caps.c (orchestrator) + cap_grant.c + cap_require.c + cap_attenuate.c.
// The split is functional (one cap-primitive per file). The shared
// state (g_tok_*, g_seal_key) lives in caps.c and is exposed as extern
// to the satellite files.
//
// v3.1.0 audit cleanup: removed cap_seal.c (the oo_cap_kernel_seal /
// oo_enclave_enter primitives had 0 callers in the umbrella; the
// sealed-cap surface is provided by app/actor/actor_rpc.c and
// sec/crypto/seal.c).
//
// ──▓▓ sec/cap ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Pillar 5 — unforgeable, kernel-derived ::
